# No per-coin hardcodes

When improving the live desk, strategies, exits, entries, or capital logic:

- **Never** special-case a single base/coin (e.g. `if base == "UNI"`, SOL-only boosts, ETH-only blocks).
- Prefer **generic** levers: thresholds, regimes, fees, util/sleeve caps, momentum/quality scores, venue economics, inventory age/depth.
- Lists like focus bases or deploy universes are OK as **config/universes**, not as one-off exception logic for one ticker.
- Comments may cite a coin as an example of why a generic threshold changed; the code path itself must stay coin-agnostic.
- If a coin looks toxic, fix via **measurable attributes** (spread, adverse selection, fill rate, AlphaI score) that apply to any symbol.
